eaching."},{"type":"h2","text":"Praise the effort, not the trait"},{"type":"p","text":"\"You worked hard on that\" grows a child who tries; \"you're so smart\" grows one who fears being wrong. The words are small; the difference compounds for years."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, agree on who owns it so it isn't quietly one person's job. Next, decide the one default that removes a daily decision. Then, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"This is exactly the kind of invisible work Bubaly was built for. Instead of holding building bedtime routines for toddlers in your head, you hand it to your family's shared system — Bubaly turns plans into real calendar events, reminders, lists, and gentle nudges, so the whole household stays in sync. Explore it at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"You'll still have messy days. That's fine. A good routine bends without breaking."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
