('the-honest-guide-to-managing-sibling-fairness-and-jealousy', 'The Honest Guide to Managing Sibling Fairness and Jealousy', 'If managing sibling fairness and jealousy has ever turned an ordinary evening into a low-grade negotiation, you are in excellent company. What follows is the approach we keep comin', 'Elena Rossi', '2024-12-24', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#parenting','#managingsibling','#parentinghacks','#lifehacks']::text[], 'Parenting', false, '#7c5dff', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/children,friends,playing?lock=1020', 'A photo related to managing sibling fairness and jealousy.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"If managing sibling fairness and jealousy has ever turned an ordinary evening into a low-grade negotiation, you are in excellent company."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Protect the wind-down"},{"type":"p","text":"The hour before bed sets the tone for the night and the morning after. Dimmer lights, lower voices, and screens away make sleep arrive on its own instead of by force."},{"type":"h2","text":"Lower the bar on purpose"},{"type":"p","text":"Perfectionism is the enemy of a warm home. A \"good enough\" dinner eaten together beats a Pinterest meal served to a stressed-out table."},{"type":"h2","text":"Model the repair, not just the rule"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids do as we do far more than as we say. If you want calm, be calm out loud: \"I'm taking a breath because I'm frustrated\" is a masterclass they'll remember."},{"type":"h2","text":"Praise the effort, not the trait"},{"type":"p","text":"\"You worked hard on that\" grows a child who tries; \"you're so smart\" grows one who fears being wrong. The words are small; the difference compounds for years."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, pick the single piece of managing sibling fairness and jealousy that causes the most friction this week. Next, add a gentle reminder so nobody has to hold it in their head. Then, decide the one default that removes a daily decision."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"Want managing sibling fairness and jealousy to run itself? That's what Bubaly does — one calm home for your family's schedule, tasks, meals, and money, with AI that stays a step ahead. Start at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"You'll still have messy days. That's fine. A good routine bends without breaking."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('everything-families-get-wrong-about-helping-kids-handle-big-feelings', 'Everything Families Get Wrong About Helping Kids Handle Big Feelings', 'The secret to helping kids handle big feelings isn''t more willpower. We''ll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and ', 'Daniel Okafor', '2025-01-10', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#parenting','#helpingkids','#momlife','#dadlife']::text[], 'Parenting', false, '#7c5dff', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/wellness,calm,nature?lock=1021', 'A photo related to helping kids handle big feelings.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"The secret to helping kids handle big feelings isn't more willpower. It's less friction — fewer decisions, clearer defaults, and a plan everyone can see."},{"type":"p","text":"We'll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and more like a shared routine."},{"type":"h2","text":"Name the feeling before the fix"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids (and adults) calm down when they feel understood, not when they're handed a solution. A quick \"you really wanted more time, huh?\" lands better than a lecture. With helping kids handle big feelings, naming the emotion first buys you the cooperation the logic needs."},{"type":"h2","text":"Siblings: coach, don't referee"},{"type":"p","text":"Stepping in to declare a winner teaches kids to recruit you as a weapon. Narrating both sides and handing the problem back — \"you two figure out a fair turn\" — builds the skill that actually ends the fighting."},{"type":"h2","text":"Connection before correction"},{"type":"p","text":"Behavior is communication. A ten-second reconnect — eye level, a hand on the shoulder, a real question — resolves more than a raised voice ever will, and it costs almost nothing."},{"type":"h2","text":"Say yes in spirit"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Yes, and we'll do it Saturday\" honors the want without breaking the boundary. Kids can wait; what they can't stand is feeling unheard."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, put it somewhere the whole family can see it. Next, decide the one default that removes a daily decision. Then, add a gentle reminder so nobody has to hold it in their head."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"Want helping kids handle big feelings to run itself? That's what Bubaly does — one calm home for your family's schedule, tasks, meals, and money, with AI that stays a step ahead. Start at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"None of this has to be perfect. Pick one idea, try it for a week, and keep only what earns its place."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
