('organizing-the-family-calendar-made-easy', 'Organizing the Family Calendar, Made Easy', 'Most families don''t struggle with organizing the family calendar because they''re doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system. What follows is the approach we', 'The Bubaly Team', '2025-03-06', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familyorganization','#organizingfamily','#familytime','#worklifebalance']::text[], 'Organization', false, '#3b82f6', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/organized,home,cleaning?lock=1077', 'A photo related to organizing the family calendar.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Most families don't struggle with organizing the family calendar because they're doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Capture, then organize"},{"type":"p","text":"The brain is for having ideas, not holding them. A single trusted inbox — one notebook, one app — where everything lands first means nothing slips through the cracks at 11pm."},{"type":"h2","text":"Declutter by the surface, not the house"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Organize the house\" is a project you'll never start. \"Clear this one counter\" is a task you'll finish before coffee. Momentum beats ambition every time."},{"type":"h2","text":"Plan the week backward"},{"type":"p","text":"Start from the fixed points — practices, appointments, work — and slot the flexible stuff around them. Planning backward from what can't move keeps the week honest."},{"type":"h2","text":"Sunday setup, ten minutes"},{"type":"p","text":"A brief weekly reset — glance at the week, prep what's needed, flag the collisions — prevents a dozen weekday scrambles. It's the highest-leverage ten minutes in the whole week."},{"type":"h2","text":"Launch pad by the door"},{"type":"p","text":"A single spot where everything t