('a-morning-routine-that-runs-itself-small-changes-big-difference', 'A Morning Routine that Runs Itself: Small Changes, Big Difference', 'The secret to a morning routine that runs itself isn''t more willpower. Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rigid program, just a handful of ideas you can borro', 'Marcus Bell', '2025-03-21', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familyorganization','#morningroutine','#lifehacks','#momlife']::text[], 'Organization', false, '#3b82f6', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/planner,calendar,desk?lock=1078', 'A photo related to a morning routine that runs itself.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"The secret to a morning routine that runs itself isn't more willpower. It's less friction — fewer decisions, clearer defaults, and a plan everyone can see."},{"type":"p","text":"Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rigid program, just a handful of ideas you can borrow tonight and adjust for your own family."},{"type":"h2","text":"The shared family calendar"},{"type":"p","text":"A schedule that lives in one person's head is a single point of failure. One calendar everyone can see — color-coded by kid — turns \"nobody told me\" into \"it's right there.\""},{"type":"h2","text":"One in, one out"},{"type":"p","text":"The fastest way to keep clutter from creeping back is a quiet trade: a new toy in, an old one out. It keeps volume flat without a single big purge."},{"type":"h2","text":"Declutter by the surface, not the house"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Organize the house\" is a project you'll never start. \"Clear this one counter\" is a task you'll finish before coffee. Momentum beats ambition every time."},{"type":"h2","text":"The five-minute tidy"},{"type":"p","text":"A timer and everyone moving beats one person resenting the mess. Five minutes of whole-family pickup before bed resets the house and shares the load fairly."},{"type":"h2","text":"Plan the week backward"},{"type":"p","text":"Start from th