('a-simple-system-for-the-ten-minute-evening-reset', 'A Simple System for The Ten-minute Evening Reset', 'Ask ten parents about the ten-minute evening reset and you''ll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh. We''ll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip,', 'The Bubaly Team', '2025-04-09', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familyorganization','#tenminuteevening','#dadlife','#momlife']::text[], 'Organization', false, '#3b82f6', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/organized,home,cleaning?lock=1079', 'A photo related to the ten-minute evening reset.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Ask ten parents about the ten-minute evening reset and you'll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh."},{"type":"p","text":"We'll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and more like a shared routine."},{"type":"h2","text":"The shared family calendar"},{"type":"p","text":"A schedule that lives in one person's head is a single point of failure. One calendar everyone can see — color-coded by kid — turns \"nobody told me\" into \"it's right there.\""},{"type":"h2","text":"A home for everything"},{"type":"p","text":"Clutter is mostly deferred decisions. When keys, backpacks, and permission slips each have one obvious home, tidying stops being a project and becomes a reflex. Start the ten-minute evening reset by deciding where things live."},{"type":"h2","text":"The five-minute tidy"},{"type":"p","text":"A timer and everyone moving beats one person resenting the mess. Five minutes of whole-family pickup before bed resets the house and shares the load fairly."},{"type":"h2","text":"Reduce the surfaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Every flat surface is a magnet for clutter. Fewer open shelves and more closed storage means less visual noise and far less to tidy."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, start smaller than feels necessary — momentum beats ambition. Next, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day. Then, give it two weeks before you judge whether it's working."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"If keeping the ten-minute evening reset on track sounds exhausting, that's the point where Bubaly quietly helps. It's the AI operating system for family life — it remembers, reminds, and coordinates so you don't have to carry it all alone. See how at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"The goal was never a flawless household. It's a calmer one — and that's absolutely within reach."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('everything-families-get-wrong-about-decluttering-the-kids-rooms-for-good', 'Everything Families Get Wrong About Decluttering the Kids'' Rooms for Good', 'Most families don''t struggle with decluttering the kids'' rooms for good because they''re doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system. What follows is the appr', 'Daniel Okafor', '2025-04-22', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familyorganization','#declutteringkids','#homelife','#organizedhome']::text[], 'Organization', false, '#3b82f6', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/organized,home,cleaning?lock=1080', 'A photo related to decluttering the kids'' rooms for good.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Most families don't struggle with decluttering the kids' rooms for good because they're doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Sunday setup, ten minutes"},{"type":"p","text":"A brief weekly reset — glance at the week, prep what's needed, flag the collisions — prevents a dozen weekday scrambles. It's the highest-leverage ten minutes in the whole week."},{"type":"h2","text":"Launch pad by the door"},{"type":"p","text":"A single spot where everything that leaves the house lives — bags, shoes, water bottles, signed forms — turns frantic mornings into a grab-and-go. What's not on the launch pad doesn't make it out."},{"type":"h2","text":"Reduce the surfaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Every flat surface is a magnet for clutter. Fewer open shelves and more closed storage means less visual noise and far less to tidy."},{"type":"h2","text":"Capture, then organize"},{"type":"p","text":"The brain is for having ideas, not holding them. A single trusted inbox — one notebook, one app — where everything lands first means nothing slips through the cracks at 11pm."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place 