('a-simple-system-for-a-fair-division-of-household-labor', 'A Simple System for A Fair Division of Household Labor', 'Most families don''t struggle with a fair division of household labor because they''re doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system. Here''s the framework, the s', 'Sofia Alvarez', '2024-10-06', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familyorganization','#fairdivision','#lifehacks','#momlife']::text[], 'Organization', false, '#3b82f6', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/planner,desk,organized?lock=1121', 'A photo related to a fair division of household labor.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Most families don't struggle with a fair division of household labor because they're doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system."},{"type":"p","text":"Here's the framework, the small habits that make it stick, and the honest caveats nobody mentions."},{"type":"h2","text":"Reduce the surfaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Every flat surface is a magnet for clutter. Fewer open shelves and more closed storage means less visual noise and far less to tidy."},{"type":"h2","text":"Defaults do the deciding"},{"type":"p","text":"Taco Tuesday exists because decisions are expensive. Standing defaults — same laundry day, same meal rhythm — free up the mental energy you were spending re-deciding the obvious."},{"type":"h2","text":"The two-minute rule"},{"type":"p","text":"If a task takes less than two minutes, do it now. Signing the form, replying to the teacher, hanging the coat — knocking these out on sight keeps the to-do list from breeding overnight."},{"type":"h2","text":"The shared family calendar"},{"type":"p","text":"A schedule that lives in one person's head is a single point of failure. One calendar everyone can see — color-coded by kid — turns \"nobody told me\" into \"it's right there.\""},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, give it two weeks before you judge whether it's workin