('everything-families-get-wrong-about-raising-kids-with-a-healthy-body-image', 'Everything Families Get Wrong About Raising Kids with a Healthy Body Image', 'Ask ten parents about raising kids with a healthy body image and you''ll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh. Here''s the framework, the small habits that make it st', 'Hannah Cho', '2026-05-28', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familywellness','#raisingkids','#familyfirst','#organizedhome']::text[], 'Wellness', false, '#f59e0b', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/wellness,calm,nature?lock=1262', 'A photo related to raising kids with a healthy body image.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Ask ten parents about raising kids with a healthy body image and you'll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh."},{"type":"p","text":"Here's the framework, the small habits that make it stick, and the honest caveats nobody mentions."},{"type":"h2","text":"Breathe before you react"},{"type":"p","text":"One slow breath creates a gap between the trigger and the response, and in that gap lives every good parenting decision you'll ever make. It's the cheapest tool with the highest return."},{"type":"h2","text":"Hydration and the afternoon slump"},{"type":"p","text":"Half of the 4pm meltdown — kids and adults — is really hunger and thirst wearing a costume. A snack and a glass of water resolve more than a timeout ever will."},{"type":"h2","text":"The 80/20 plate"},{"type":"p","text":"Nutrition isn't all-or-nothing. Aim for mostly-good most of the time and let dessert be dessert. The pressure to be perfect causes more harm at the table than the occasional cookie."},{"type":"h2","text":"Model the repair with yourself"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids learn self-care by watching. When they see you rest without guilt, apologize without shame, and ask for help without drama, you teach more than any lecture could."},{"type":"h2","text":"Connection is medicine"},{"type":"p","text":"Loneliness is a he