('teaching-kids-healthy-screen-boundaries-without-the-overwhelm', 'Teaching Kids Healthy Screen Boundaries Without the Overwhelm', 'Most families don''t struggle with teaching kids healthy screen boundaries because they''re doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system. What follows is the ap', 'The Bubaly Team', '2024-09-02', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familywellness','#teachingkids','#lifehacks','#homelife']::text[], 'Wellness', false, '#f59e0b', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/technology,child,tablet?lock=1278', 'A photo related to teaching kids healthy screen boundaries.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Most families don't struggle with teaching kids healthy screen boundaries because they're doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Sunlight and outside time"},{"type":"p","text":"Ten minutes of morning light sets the body clock; time outdoors resets the mood. It's free, it's fast, and it does more for the whole family than most supplements."},{"type":"h2","text":"Protect white space"},{"type":"p","text":"An over-scheduled family is a stressed family. Guarding a few blank evenings a week isn't laziness; it's maintenance. Rest is where the recovery actually happens."},{"type":"h2","text":"Breathe before you react"},{"type":"p","text":"One slow breath creates a gap between the trigger and the response, and in that gap lives every good parenting decision you'll ever make. It's the cheapest tool with the highest return."},{"type":"h2","text":"The 80/20 plate"},{"type":"p","text":"Nutrition isn't all-or-nothing. Aim for mostly-good most of the time and let dessert be dessert. The pressure to be perfect causes more harm at the table than the occasional cookie."},{"type":"h2","text":"Less news, more presence"},{"type":"p","text":"A household marinating in headlines carries a background hum of dread. Curating the input — and being present instead of scrolling — lowers the whole family's baseline stress."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, decide the one default that removes a daily decision. Next, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day. Then, pick the single piece of teaching kids healthy screen boundaries that causes the most friction this week."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"If keeping teaching kids healthy screen boundaries on track sounds exhausting, that's the point where Bubaly quietly helps. It's the AI operating system for family life — it remembers, reminds, and coordinates so you don't have to carry it all alone. See how at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"Start small, stay consistent, and let the system do the remembering so you don't have to."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('building-a-gratitude-practice-that-sticks-that-actually-sticks', 'Building a Gratitude Practice that Sticks That Actually Sticks', 'The secret to building a gratitude practice that sticks isn''t more willpower. Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rigid program, just a handful of ideas you ca', 'The Bubaly Team', '2024-09-20', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familywellness','#buildinggratitude','#familytime','#homelife']::text[], 'Wellness', false, '#f59e0b', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/sports,children,activity?lock=1279', 'A photo related to building a gratitude practice that sticks.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"The secret to building a gratitude practice that sticks isn't more willpower. It's less friction — fewer decisions, clearer defaults, and a plan everyone can see."},{"type":"p","text":"Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rigid program, just a handful of ideas you can borrow tonight and adjust for your own family."},{"type":"h2","text":"Connection is medicine"},{"type":"p","text":"Loneliness is a health risk; belonging is a buffer. Regular, low-stakes togetherness — a shared meal, a standing walk — does quiet, measurable good for everyone under the roof."},{"type":"h2","text":"Name the mental load"},{"type":"p","text":"The invisible work of noticing, planning, and remembering is real work, and it exhausts the person carrying it. Saying it out loud is the first step to sharing it."},{"type":"h2","text":"Breathe before you react"},{"type":"p","text":"One slow breath creates a gap between the trigger and the response, and in that gap lives every good parenting decision you'll ever make. It's the cheapest tool with the highest return."},{"type":"h2","text":"Model the repair with yourself"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids learn self-care by watching. When they see you rest without guilt, apologize without shame, and ask for help without drama, you teach more than any lecture could."},{"type":"h2","t