('building-a-kid-friendly-dinner-rotation-without-the-overwhelm', 'Building a Kid-friendly Dinner Rotation Without the Overwhelm', 'Building a Kid-friendly Dinner Rotation is one of those quietly relentless parts of family life: never urgent enough to fix, never small enough to ignore. Here''s the framework, the', 'Nina Patel', '2026-03-31', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familymeals','#buildingkidfriendly','#homelife','#momlife']::text[], 'Recipes & Food', false, '#f97316', 'https://loremflickr.com/1600/900/cooking,kitchen,food?lock=1418', 'A photo related to building a kid-friendly dinner rotation.', 'LoremFlickr (CC)', $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Building a Kid-friendly Dinner Rotation is one of those quietly relentless parts of family life: never urgent enough to fix, never small enough to ignore."},{"type":"p","text":"Here's the framework, the small habits that make it stick, and the honest caveats nobody mentions."},{"type":"h2","text":"Prep components, not full meals"},{"type":"p","text":"Cooked grains, roasted veg, and a protein in the fridge become five different dinners. Prepping building blocks beats cooking five separate meals and keeps leftovers from feeling like leftovers."},{"type":"h2","text":"The list builds itself"},{"type":"p","text":"A meal plan and a grocery list are the same document. Write the plan, and the list falls out of it — sorted by aisle, minus what's already in the pantry."},{"type":"h2","text":"Leftovers, reinvented"},{"type":"p","text":"Last night's roast chicken is tonight's tacos and tomorrow's soup. Treating leftovers as ingredients, not repeats, slashes waste and the mental load at once."},{"type":"h2","text":"Cook once, eat twice"},{"type":"p","text":"Double the batch, freeze half. A little extra effort tonight buys you a free dinner on the worst night of next week — the cheapest insurance in the kitchen."},{"type":"h2","text":"A well-stocked pantry is a safety net"},{"type":"p","text":"When the fridge looks empty, a good pantry still has dinner in it. A handful of staples — pasta, beans, tinned tomatoes, rice — means you're never truly stuck."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, decide the one default that removes a daily decision. Next, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day. Then, give it two weeks before you judge whether it's working."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"Bubaly was designed for moments exactly like this: it takes building a kid-friendly dinner rotation off your mental to-do list and turns it into shared, automatic routines the whole family can see. Learn more at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"You'll still have messy days. That's fine. A good routine bends without breaking."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
